WEBVTT

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:11.900
♪ This is our quartet... ♪

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.660
These lyrics that strike my crimson soul...

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.330
No matter how many times
I hear them, they're the best!

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:24.960
Crap, I think I might
fall in love with myself...

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:30.760
Foolish rodent, it is true
folly that you are so mistaken.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.550
Your lyrics are no more than an accessory

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.720
to the sublime melodies
by me, the only dark god.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.100
What did you say?

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.720
Which is the "accessory"?

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.810
Your songs are like the fermented
bamboo shoots on top of ramen!

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.190
You dwarf, if that's the case,
then your lyrics are chopped green onions!

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.570
Which are bigger? Fermented bamboo
shoots or chopped green onions?

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.530
Shut up!

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.030
Why am I included in this?!

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.280
Jeez, why are you guys always fighting?!

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:01.290
Is this really the time to be
fighting about who's better?

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.790
We should be evaluating our
new song right now, for real.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.290
Don't you agree?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.800
As expected of a man with a full-time job.
His words are persuasive!

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.720
That's true. Well, what should we do, Rom?

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.470
About that—

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.100
I happened to overhear

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:24.390
about a hot new spot for street performances!

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.320
<i>Ready... 1, 2, 3, GO!</i>

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.160
<i>Love life! Very! Very! Happy!</i>

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.950
<i>Friendship life! Bouncing, jumping!</i>

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.660
<i>Adventure life! Heart-pounding, OK?</i>

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.630
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:54.260
<i>Rushing out onto the road to</i>
<i>school with the blue sky behind us</i>

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.220
<i>I like that! I like this, too!</i>

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.720
<i>I'll take it all, all of it~</i>

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:02.600
<i>A girl who imagines love is all romance</i>

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.350
<i>If I can attack, I'll do it boldly</i>

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.980
<i>Let's find an original vision for the future</i>

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:15.900
<i>Sometimes, we'll have a secret love advice time</i>

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.740
<i>Who do you like?</i>

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:26.290
<i>You've got a green light for love now!</i>
<i>It's your chance to move forward!</i>

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.120
<i>So, let's just</i>

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.130
<i>Have a blast! Fall in love!</i>

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.210
<i>Our youth is non-stop!</i>

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.300
<i>Run! Aim for the future!</i>

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:35.920
<i>Everyone gather</i>

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.800
<i>For a happy ending!</i>

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.350
<i>Will tomorrow be happy or sad?</i>
<i>Will we idle our time away?</i>

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.430
<i>We'll work hard!</i>

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.730
<i>I want to keep dreaming forever!</i>

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.940
<i>Let's fly out into the</i>
<i>world with all our strength!</i>

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:54.820
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.450
Yokai Street?

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:05.410
Yeah, it's where our band,
Shinimonogurui, is based.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:11.630
There's talk online about how amazing
bands have surprise concerts there.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:17.920
It's true that different bands have
gathered there because of those rumors.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.300
At the same time, monsters have
started appearing more often, too.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:27.060
In the midst of that, one of your
members, Tsugihagi, has gone missing?

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.730
Marimari!

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.730
Where have you gone, Tsugihagi...?

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:42.820
So you want us to help you find Tsugihagi?

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.200
That's right.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.870
But, why us?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.670
During Trichron's concert at BooDooKan,
I saw Cyan's performance and thought,

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.330
maybe she can do something!

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.800
Oh, um, that was...

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:01.130
It would be comforting to have you all there.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.640
Please, help me!

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:14.560
All right. We'll do what we can!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.620
This is where we live—Yokai Street.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.800
This is where we of the
<i>yokai</i> race make our home.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.550
I didn't know there was a race like that...

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.720
I didn't either, pyuru.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.980
All <i>yokai</i> love pranks,
but they're all good-natured.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.650
There's no need to worry at all!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.280
Gold is nice...

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.700
It never talks idly or defies you.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.250
It is always obedient.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:14.580
What is it?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.880
They fell for it! They fell for it!

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.800
It is completely obedient,
and it satisfies my heart.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.600
D-Dagger, sir.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.930
They have fallen for my plan.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.270
Will you tell me in a way that I can understand?

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.850
Yes, sir!

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:41.900
First, I spread rumors about how amazing
bands were performing in Yokai Street.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.950
From there, bands started
gathering one after another.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.410
And then?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:54.620
Sir, I did not expect this, but the girl,
Cyan, is in Yokai Street right now.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:59.590
I see... I will leave that to you.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.210
What?! Leave it to me?

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:06.840
I'm saying that you're getting a
chance to make up for your failures so far.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.050
Th-Thank you very much, sir!

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:13.930
I will definitely do everything I can to
live up to your expectations this time, sir!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.730
Like I'll let you.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:28.240
We'll overtake Tsurezure soon, don't you think?

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:34.120
We're getting rich! At this rate,
it's not a dream for us to become first!

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.790
The winds are in our favor!

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.420
It's not like I didn't expect it, though.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:43.380
There it is! Rosia's acting overconfident again!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:48.930
But I mean, we're a band with the
world-famous Unicorn Virtual Music.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:52.970
If you think about our talents
and the power of our label,

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.310
wouldn't it be strange if we
<i>didn't</i> surpass Tsurezure and Trichron

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.020
and take the top spot in a week or two?

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.850
That confidence is reassuring.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.980
If it wasn't, then it'd be a lie.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.280
This is the entrance?

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.080
It's pretty plain.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:20.210
No, I believe it's rather elegant. Hence—

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:26.170
I suppose you can say it is sufficient
to test the skills of a malevolent god.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.550
It's like a haunted house.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.430
All right, let's go!

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.940
This is a creepy town, for real.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.150
It looks like something
could pop out any minute—

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.530
You guys, hurry up and get over here!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.280
Oi, Aion, you go first...!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.000
The great sun god of
darkness is suited to go last.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.080
Then, Yaiba! You go!

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.790
I will take this opportunity to follow the
teachings of the Way of Ryukomuso Kamui

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.260
and take the rear guard. Hence—

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.550
Stop messing around, you bastards!

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.340
Excuse me...

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:19.270
Hello.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:26.480
Jeez, those guys...
They've got no guts, as usual.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.070
What?!

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.070
What the—

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:43.790
I was just trying to greet them...

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.800
Hey, what happened?

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.670
Wh-What was that just now...?

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:56.470
Th-Th-Th-Th-The heart
of this sun god of darkness

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:00.310
did not quiver in the slightest
from the silly actions of a <i>yokai.</i>

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:06.900
Something like this does not even
require me to draw my Ryukenden. Hence—

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.780
Oh, there's a perfect chair here!

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.030
I will rest for a moment.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:14.400
Hence!

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:16.910
Yaiba, what's wrong?!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.330
Things are getting interesting!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:30.840
Anyway, isn't this like a haunted
house at a seedy amusement park?

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.630
H-Hence, this is absurd!

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:36.430
That's so lame, Aion!

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:39.260
You need to make sure you've
got a good grip on yourself like me—

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.060
What the heck is this—?!

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:50.480
Mon, mon, mon, mon, mon... Mon, mon!

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.370
Why don't I play with you a little?

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:10.040
But do you have reason to
believe Tsugihagi is still in town?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.010
No, I don't...

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:16.800
But Tsugihagi has a gentle personality,

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:20.600
and I can't think that he
would leave this town on his own.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.310
He was anxious about something, though.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:32.270
He wanted to become better at
playing the keyboard, his instrument.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.900
So he was worried about something?

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.740
I should have listened to
what he had to say more seriously.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:45.660
All the band members regret that so much!

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:49.250
I want to see him again and apologize...

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:51.920
Tsugihagi...

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:02.050
Don't bands bond over incidents like this?

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.770
We had our share in the past, too... Right?

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.440
We had a big fight just a little while ago.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:12.480
Our band was on the verge of breaking up, pyuru!

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.820
Wow! Good job overcoming that!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:20.450
Yes, without that, we wouldn't
be who we are right now.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:23.700
So, I'm sure it'll be
true for your band, too...!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.910
Oh, that Tsugihagi.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:34.170
I swear, if he's just hiding timidly somewhere,
I'm going to give him a good scolding.

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:38.760
Cyan!

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:40.050
Mr. Berry?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.260
It looks like danger's coming.

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.970
What? Don't tell me...

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:47.640
Yeah. It's a monster!

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:51.440
Marimari, where do you
usually have your concerts?

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.940
At the Ushimitsu Plaza!

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.570
Will you take us there?

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:11.000
This is it, huh? Ushimitsu Plaza?

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:13.000
We finally made it...

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:19.880
If our journey here was like that, I shudder
to think of our journey back. Hence—

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:24.890
By the time it's time for us to leave,
all the residents here will be my cattle!

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:26.260
Let's go...

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.370
Listen, you cattle!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.710
We are wild soldiers who
run through crimson battlefields!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:55.040
SHINGANCRIMSONZ!

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:01.760
All right, go dark monster!

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.640
Wh-What's that?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.910
Hey, hurry up and get off me, you guys!

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.420
I believe we were just on the concert stage.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.510
Don't tell me this is the work of the <i>yokai</i>?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:43.920
What?

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:54.390
Wh-What's that?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.070
Damn it...!

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.540
So this is a dark monster?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.130
Don't tell me Tsugihagi
was also attacked by this...?

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.750
Don't think about that, pyuru!

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:24.670
Cyan, let's go!

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:25.920
Okay!

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.220
I can't get in!

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.140
A barrier, huh?

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.350
Too bad!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:43.900
Just watch, Cyan. Once I bring
down these guys, it'll be your turn next!

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:46.950
Oi, bastard! What are you trying to do?!

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:51.580
Today's an important day! We were
going to reveal our new song at this concert!

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:54.040
I don't know what grudge you bear,

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.330
but don't get in the way of our performance!

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:02.500
Foolish <i>yokai</i>. I will absolutely
not allow this blasphemy!

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:07.630
I have lost my patience with you. Hence—!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:13.310
Shut up and carve the screams
of our souls into your heart!

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.810
I summon Red Tomahawk!

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:21.190
Receive the holy thunderbolt of darkness!

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.900
I summon Holy Ark!

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:31.320
I'll show you the mysteries of
the Way of Ryukomuso Kamui...

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.990
Come, Ryukenden!

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.830
Let's go, guys!

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:50.880
<i>My sixth sense released my mind's eye</i>

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:54.720
<i>Letting a gunshot ring at this faltering world</i>

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:55.430
Damn it!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:55.640
<i>Letting a gunshot ring at this faltering world</i>

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:56.600
Take off that giant thing
you're wearing on your head!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:01.350
<i>The burning bullet is under the name of Crimson</i>

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:06.610
<i>Yes... I'll perform a capriccio to lead you all</i>

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.150
<i>I swear loyalty</i>

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.070
Go to hell, <i>yokai</i>!

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.280
<i>Connected by chains...</i>

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:18.870
You guys!

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.410
Mr. Berry!

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:24.130
We have no choice but
to leave this to those guys!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.930
You're pretty strong for a <i>yokai...</i>

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.470
I'll have to get serious and—

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:43.940
Seriously?

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:54.570
Rom?

00:16:54.780 --> 00:17:02.370
We are going to carve a burning
crimson legend of music in Midi City as one!

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.670
We can't let a guy like this
get in the way of our concert!

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.130
Rom...

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:12.880
We've gotta get serious
about this, too! That is our reality!

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.220
Yeah!

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:33.030
<i>My sixth sense released my mind's eye</i>

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:38.410
<i>Letting a gunshot ring at this faltering world</i>

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:42.870
Face the supreme judgment of god!

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:43.660
<i>The burning bullet is under the name of Crimson</i>

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.750
<i>Yes... I'll perform a capriccio to lead you all</i>

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.590
Playtime is over! Hence—!

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:48.710
<i>Yes... I'll perform a capriccio to lead you all</i>

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:51.340
<i>I swear loyalty</i>

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:56.260
<i>Connected by chains</i>

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:59.390
<i>Listen to this song that will reclaim that fettered body</i>

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.930
Take that!

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:06.940
<i>Yes... Blossom vividly and in full glory</i>

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:12.530
<i>This is our quartet...</i>

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:24.540
We will continue gazing at this faltering
world with the crimson eyes of our heart.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:27.170
SHINGANCRIMSONZ!

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.340
Wow... amazing!

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.130
They defeated it!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.300
A huge victory, pyuru!

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.340
Not bad...

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.350
Those guys...

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.970
They did it.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.450
Hence!

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:04.870
I stole the spotlight today, too!

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.160
They rained down, pyuru!

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.370
They're back!

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.170
Tsugihagi!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:20.390
Stupid Tsugihagi...!

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:23.600
Sorry, Marimari...

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:28.020
No, I have to apologize, too.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.980
I should have listened to what you had to say.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.360
Thanks.

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:36.230
I'm glad you found Tsugihagi.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:39.150
But I don't understand...

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:44.660
Tsugihagi was the dark monster?
How in the world did that happen?

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.670
I remember being worried
about something, but...

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:55.750
Well, it's fine! The important
thing is that you're back!

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:59.590
It was thanks to these people saving you!

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:03.760
Go on, Tsugihagi.

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.890
U-Um... Here...

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.230
Huh? What's this?

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:14.110
It's <i>konpeito</i> candy to thank you.

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.770
Huh? What? <i>Kon... pei... to...</i>?

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.740
Just take it, Crow.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.360
Does this taste good?

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:31.750
What's wrong?

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:34.290
Something, just now...

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:39.380
Marimari! Tsugihagi!

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:40.420
Those guys...!

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.970
The <i>yokai</i> from earlier!

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:44.970
They're our bandmates!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.300
Huh?

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.100
Bandmates?!

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:49.640
Thank you!

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.390
Come back to visit!

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.020
See you later, pyuru!

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:00.030
No way!

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:03.660
We were fighting a dark monster?!

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.160
You fought it without knowing?

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:12.000
We thought it was one
of the <i>yokai</i> trying to scare us.

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:14.420
If they knew, they might not have won.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:16.170
I agree, pyuru!

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:20.670
I see... We defeated a dark monster...

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.970
I'm so amazing!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:28.640
Even so, for the missing band
member to be the dark monster...

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:30.720
Yeah.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:36.440
I wonder if the dark monsters are
attacking band members indiscriminately...?

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.110
It's a little scary...

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:45.240
That Tsugihagi was worried about
his performance or something, right?

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.410
Yeah...

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:50.990
Darkness in one's heart and
turning into a dark monster...

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.540
Are they related somehow?

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:04.130
<i>If you like it, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:07.010
<i>You can do it because you like it</i>

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:09.720
<i>The feeling that you like music</i>

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:13.100
<i>Can't be stopped by anyone</i>

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:21.520
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:23.740
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:27.280
<i>Running through my body</i>

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:29.820
<i>This electric thrill</i>

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:34.830
<i>Is this feeling curiosity?</i>

00:22:35.960 --> 00:22:38.370
<i>Negativity is a decrescendo</i>

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:41.040
<i>Hope and expectations, a crescendo</i>

00:22:41.250 --> 00:22:46.590
<i>Show off our passion and</i>
<i>get god to be our ally, too</i>

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:52.100
<i>I wanna share with everyone and have a taste of</i>

00:22:52.310 --> 00:22:55.810
<i>Big!! Rocking!! Heart-throbbing!! Happiness!!!!</i>

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:59.850
<i>If it's you, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:02.860
<i>You can do it because it's you</i>

00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:07.950
<i>Let's try performing these</i>
<i>dream-colored notes together</i>

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:11.160
<i>I want to tell you directly</i>

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:13.990
<i>A life-sized, "heart-sized" heart</i>

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:16.870
<i>In order for it to reach you...</i>

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:20.210
<i>I will sing with all I have</i>

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:22.960
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:24.920
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:28.340
What? You're saying Aion seems kind of down?

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:30.180
Yeah, even though at Chinchikurin,

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:33.260
that guy usually gets so much garlic in his
tonkotsu ramen you can't see the surface,

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:35.430
he only put three spoonfuls in last time.

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:37.180
Unbelievable! Something's gotta be wrong!

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:38.520
Maybe he's feeling sick.

00:23:38.730 --> 00:23:40.690
Hm? That's a normal amount. A normal amount!
